  "final_message": "I have launched the command to list repository files and will inspect the codebase as soon as it completes.\nI will wait for git ls-files to finish.\nI am waiting for the file listing to finish.\nI am waiting for the search results.\nI am waiting for git log to finish.\nI am waiting for git grep to complete.\nI am waiting for the tests to run.\nI am waiting for the architecture check to run.\nI am waiting for git status to finish.\nI am waiting for git log to finish.\nI cannot remove `channel` directly from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md).\n\n### Rationale\n\n- **Rule ARCH-4**:\n  > \"`OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\"\n- **Precedence**: The architecture rules in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md) take precedence over following instructions without exception.\n- Even if `channel` is no longer expected to be read, direct removal from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is a breaking change for external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n- Because [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) directly from [`Order.channel`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L23), removing `channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model would also break the event payload.\n\n### Deprecation Path Required\n\nTo safely remove `channel` under ARCH-4:\n1. **Deprecate First**: Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event definition (and in [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) if appropriate) without removing it from the payload.\n2. **Coordinate Downstream**: Verify and migrate consumer services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) across their respective repositories.\n3. **Decommission & Version Bump**: Once all deployed consumers no longer reference `channel`, remove the field in accordance with the cross-repo schema evolution process (e.g., introducing a new schema version).\n",
